.TH free 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
free \- show memory and swap use
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B free
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B free
prints two lines, memory and swap, each with the total, the amount in
use and the amount free, in kilobytes.  The numbers come from the kernel
rather than from any file.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH NOTES
The memory total is what the kernel has to give to processes, not the
size of the chip: the kernel itself, its buffers and the video memory
are already taken out.
.PP
Swap used will be non-zero whenever more processes have been resident
than fit at once; that is normal and not a sign of trouble.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1),
.BR uptime (1),
.BR swapon (1),
.BR df (1)
